[[Queens of Mischief Cosmetic Pack|QoM]] Soulvester has armor colored a faded purple hue and mint green arms. The ponytail-esque piece of his helmet is mint colored with a gradually whitening end and appears more hair-like, being made up of multiple strands. More jagged, greener strands also poke out from the top of the piece slightly towards the right, the left side of the piece, and a much smaller one underneath the piece. He sports large, dark purple headphones with lighter ear cushions, gleaming outer shells, and a microphone speaker attached to the boom on the left. Replacing his breastplate is a magenta tee-shirt with the [[Queens of Mischief]] logo, except it has a darker fade on the upper and lower parts of it instead of a checker pattern. He wears a green and magenta glow bracelet on each of his hands and feet, specifically in that order except for his left leg with the order reversed. When moving, he leaves behind three different trails, all of which have a mint to magenta gradient and are transparent. One is a wavy pair of measures divided in three sections. The upper measure has a treble clef, whole rest, quarter rest, beamed eighth note on the "B" line and "E" space, and a tie for the first section. The second section has a quarter note on the "E" space, another quarter note on the same space, an eighth note on the "D" line, and a dotted quarter note on the "B" line. For the third section, a quarter rest, eighth rest, eighth note on the "B" line, and a sixteenth note with its first head on the "D" line, its second head on the "C" space, and its other heads on the "B" line. The lower measure is similar to the upper, except for the first section, the beamed eighth note is positioned two lines lower and has a natural. For the second section, the quarter note is on the "G" line, the next quarter note is on the "A” space, the eighth note is on the "B" line, and the dotted quarter note is on the "G" line and has a natural. For the third section, the last two notes are lowered by three lines. The other trails are a bouncing group of quarter notes, beamed eighth notes, and beamed sixteenth notes and a cross-bone pattern.
