==Personality==
Soulvester is a [[Toon]] who accurately lines up with a real knight, speaking perfectly fluent Early Modern English and having a heroic nature. He even shrugs off claims about him not being a real knight and takes offense whenever his behavior gets referred to as dorky. He's often seen offering help to the other Toons, whether it's providing them with protection, gathering supplies or just giving them general advice, but he's oddly quick to turn down any help offered to him, likely lining up with his heroism (but he gets quite defensive when asked to remove his armor for mundane reasons). This knightly attitude is especially apparent towards {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}, as Soulvester tries to protect him from the cruel reality and circumstances he and the other Toons have been subjected to, such as not being able to protect Gourdy or his parents from losing each other.

Unlike with the other related Toons, Soulvester's relationship with his twin sister {{CI|Connie|name=true}} is on worse terms, to the point where he seems to actually be glad to see her less often. He does not however like when other Toons such as {{CI|Teagan|name=true}} speak lowly of Connie, showing that the ghostly duo does in fact care for each other, just like how the others do (although it is shown even less than it would traditionally be).

In summary, Soulvester may be tough and heroic, acting intensely accurately to a real knight, but all armor pieces have something inside of them.

