==Trivia==
*Soulvester and {{CI|Connie|name=true}} being twin siblings<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1424041671519240273</ref> makes them the fifth set of [[Toons]] with a canonical biological relationship.
*Soulvester has longer hair than [[Connie|his sister]], meaning that he has the longest hair in-game.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1423184461918371891</ref>
**Despite this, in one piece of halloween decor in the [[Lobby]], Soulvester's helmet is placed with his "hair" on it like a plume.
*Soulvester is the first non-{{Type|Main}} [[Holiday Toon]] to have 5 {{Star}} in two [[Stats]] (Extraction and Skill Check).
**He also shares these stats with {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}.
**He and Gourdy are also the only Toons to have 1 Star in two Stats, while having a normal amount of Stars.
***He is the first non-Main Character Event Toon to have 1 Star on a Stat.
**This also makes him the seventh non-Main Character Toon to have 5 Stars in a Stat.
*Soulvester is the second [[Toon]] to wear footwear by default, after {{CI|Dyle|name=true}}, the second Toon to wear gloves by default, after [[Blot]], and the third Toon to wear some type of head accessory by default, after {{CI|Astro|name=true}} & {{CI|Poppy|name=true}}, and [[Connie]].
*Soulvester's name is a portmanteau of the word "Soul", "Vessel", and the name Sylvester.
*In one of Soulvester's dialogues with [[Connie]] and {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}, they mention that he is "larping as a knight", which implies he is not actually one. Even if he may not actually be one, he seems to have a heavy belief otherwise, due to his protective nature and the fact he wears armor.
*Soulvester's low Movement Speed and Stamina is due to his heavy armor, as stated in an interaction between him and {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}}. His low Movement Speed could also reference his [[Connie|sister]]'s speed.
*For some odd reason, before a certain update, {{Skin|Vintage Soulvester}} glowed the same color as his default [[Skin]] (being cyan) instead of white. This would've made him the only Light-Producing [[Toon]] that glows a different color that isn't white in his Vintage Skin.
**Similarly, this was also the case for his {{Skin|Golden Knight}} where it glowed cyan before being given a more suitable golden glow.
*Soulvester is the second [[Holiday Toon]] to appear in the thumbnail not escaping from a [[Twisted]], instead giving {{CI|Twisted Gourdy|name=true}} a {{II|Stealth Candy|name=true}}.
*Soulvester is the second [[Toon]] with 2 [[Auxiliary Stat]]<nowiki/>s (Light-Production and [[Ichor Puddle]] Immunity), akin to his [[Connie|sister]] who has the same Aux. Stats.
**He is also the only [[Event Toon]] with this trait.
*Soulvester is the first [[Toon]] to:
**Have custom music playing while his [[Ability]] is active.
**Have a stun Ability.
***This was something [[Qwel]] actually pushed back on, due to it ruining the danger of facing [[Twisteds]].<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1340011638941683765</ref>
**Be able to bring a Toon's [[Health]] above their usual maximum, as {{AI|Soulvester|name=true}} adds an extra, blue heart to the targets Health, regardless of if they're already at max.
**Have a selfless Ability that becomes a selfish counterpart in solos.
*Prior to his rework in the [[2026 Halloween Event]], Soulvester was the only [[Toon]] to have 4 {{Heart}} due to his original [[Ability]] giving him an extra Heart along with being immune to some ranged attacks.
**However, if you equip the {{TI|Soul Sword|name=true}} on him, Soulvester's heart total will be increased back to the previous 4 Hearts, though immunity to {{CI|Twisted Scraps|name=true}} and {{CI|Twisted Goob|name=true}}'s ranged attacks only returns when he uses his [[Ability]] in a solo run.
*Soulvester is the second [[Toon]] to have an [[Ability]] category change (Passive to Active), the first being {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}.
**Both of them had their Abilities change into an Active Ability.
*As [[Aaron]] stated on his X account, the book Soulvester is looking for in his interaction with {{CI|Squirm|name=true}} is 'Le Morte d'Arthur' (The Death of Arthur) by Sir Thomas Malory.<ref>https://x.com/Aaron_Margolin/status/2114076843209007379</ref>
*Soulvester shares the same smoke-like particle effect with [[Connie]], the difference being that it appears when he teleports, while hers appears when she turns invisible.
*Soulvester has the second lowest [[Ability]] cooldown at only 3 seconds, being beat by {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, who has 0 seconds.
**This is likely at least one of the reasons {{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}} and {{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}} don't reduce his cooldown.
*Soulvester has the most complex singular [[Ability]] by far, as it has many mechanics to it:
**The {{Debuff|HurtBurst}} [[Buff]] he gets from being hit by a [[Twisted]];
**The {{Debuff|GuardStance|I}} Buff he gets from using his Ability;
**The {{Debuff|Guarded}} Buff he can give to another [[Toon]];
**The stun he gives to Twisteds after defending a Guarded Toon;
**The {{Debuff|GuardBurst}} and {{Debuff|Untargetable}} Buffs he gets after defending a Guarded Toon;
**The teleportation and cutscene he does when defending a Guarded Toon that isn't himself;
**Tracking whether a Toon is in a chase or not.
*When Soulvester's [[Ability]] first got reworked, it was possible for him to teleport out of the [[Elevator]] to stun [[Twisteds]] during [[Panic Mode]]. This was later changed so that he can't teleport if he's inside the Elevator during Panic Mode, due to the unfair possibility of Soulvester not being able to get back in the Elevator in time after stunning a Twisted.
*Soulvester is the first non-[[Main Character]]/{{Type|Lethal}} to have an interactable NPC counterpart (albeit without dialogue).
**NPC Soulvester uses the Rock Out emote on loop there, but when you use 'Start Band' as any [[Toon]] from the [[Queens of Mischief Cosmetic Pack]], if he is in the ring, he will automatically join your band and dance, despite not being an actual player. Ending it reverts him back to Rock Out.
*Soulvester is the second [[Toon]] to have the capability to teleport, the first being {{CI|Glisten|name=true}}.
**However, while Glisten can teleport at the user's input, Soulvester has to guard a Toon and have them get hit so Soulvester teleports to their position (assuming that Soulvester isn't in the [[Elevator]] during [[Panic Mode]]).
*In the [[Soundtrack|Queens Of Mischief]] music video, Soulvester has a texturing error where his arms become gray instead of teal.
*Soulvester is currently the only [[Toon]] to have an [[Ability]] that purely increases in full Stars rather than a percentage boost.
**{{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}'s Ability seemingly increases by Stars, but while it does affect [[Movement Speed]] (15) by 2 Stars, [[Extraction Speed]] (1.125) changes by 0.375 units, not a full Star value. Soulvester only increases by the defined value per Star (2.5 units per Star for Movement Speed).
*Soulvester's printable [[Haunted Gala]] mask has an error where the dark rectangle surrounding his eyes disappear.
**Additionally, his name was written incorrectly, being called "Soulvestor".
*Soulvester (and effectively {{CI|Ribecca|name=true}}) is the only [[Toons]] to get [[Ichor Puddle]] Immunity after its release.

